### TopUp Wallet — Wallet.Api
### The money core: accounts, idempotent credit/debit, ledger, audit.
### Run top-to-bottom: later requests reuse the account id from "createAccount"
### via a request variable, so you don't copy/paste ids.
###
### Container run maps the service to :5001 (compose). Local `dotnet run` picks
### its own port from launchSettings — override @host below if needed.

@host = http://localhost:5001
@contentType = application/json

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

###
# @name createAccount
### Create an account opening with $100. The @name lets later requests read its
### response (the generated account id).
POST {{host}}/accounts
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "ownerName": "Ada Lovelace",
  "currency": "USD",
  "opening": 100
}

###
@accountId = {{createAccount.response.body.$.id}}

### Fetch the account
GET {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}

### Credit $50 (idempotencyKey is REQUIRED and must be unique per real operation)
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/credit
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "amount": 50,
  "idempotencyKey": "credit-001"
}

### Debit $30
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/debit
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "amount": 30,
  "idempotencyKey": "debit-001"
}

### Idempotency demo — REPLAY the same debit key.
### Expect: wasReplay=true, SAME transactionId, balance unchanged (charged once).
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/debit
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "amount": 30,
  "idempotencyKey": "debit-001"
}

### Insufficient funds — debit more than the balance.
### Expect: 400 { "error": "insufficient_funds" }, balance untouched.
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/debit
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "amount": 999999,
  "idempotencyKey": "debit-overdraw"
}

### Validation — non-positive amount is rejected (400).
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/credit
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "amount": 0,
  "idempotencyKey": "credit-zero"
}

### Immutable ledger (SQL Server) — newest first.
GET {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/transactions

### Audit trail (MongoDB) — append-only event log.
GET {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/audit

### Not found — unknown account id.
GET {{host}}/accounts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
